deflate_bench: measuring compression throughput and per-stream memory: the Rust port against the in-process C oracle.
deflate_bench:   per-case lines are `RATIO group=... case=... bytes=... port_ns=... oracle_ns=... ratio=... ratio_hi=... rounds=... order=... limit=... gate=counted|informational verdict=within|over` and `MEMORY group=... case=... port_bytes=... oracle_bytes=... ratio=... limit=... verdict=within|over`; then exactly one `RATIO-SUMMARY`/`MEMORY-SUMMARY` line per declared group, carrying `gate=authoritative|supporting|informational` and `expected=<cases the group set out to measure>` -- a group with nothing to measure still prints its line, with `expected=0` -- and one `ALLOC-BALANCE` line per side per memory case. Reported, never enforced -- the workflow decides.
deflate_bench: GATE-INVENTORY suite=deflate ratio_limit=1.10 memory_limit=1.15 min_bytes=4096 levels=1,6,9 authoritative_ratio=deflate_steady_state,deflate_silesia supporting_ratio=deflate_lifecycle,deflate_container,deflate_feeding,compress_oneshot informational_ratio=deflate_mem_level,deflate_strategy,deflate_stored_floor,deflate_bound,deflate_degenerate authoritative_memory=deflate_memory
deflate_bench: CRITERION root=/synthetic/target/criterion port_label=zlib-rs oracle_label=c-oracle layout=<root>/<group>/<label>/<case>/new/estimates.json estimate=slope fallback=mean authority=criterion self_timed=diagnostic registration=alternating rounds=9 order=alternating
